event: response.completed
data: {"response":{"background":false,"completed_at":1791532666,"created_at":1791532666,"error":null,"frequency_penalty":0,"id":"resp_922778","incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"max_output_tokens":null,"max_tool_calls":null,"metadata":{},"model":"gpt-oss:120b","object":"response","output":[{"encrypted_content":"Everything seems correct. Why tests timed out? Possibly because Playwright expects elements to have role attributes. The heading \u003ch1\u003e default role heading, fine.\n\nBut maybe the root page not loaded due to SPA navigation interfering with Playwright navigation? They navigate to '/' and then expect heading visible. That should be fine.\n\nThe test also expects that after creating project and reload, the row persists. That should work.\n\nPotential issue: In index.html, the input has aria-label but also label element with for attribute. Role textbox detection uses label text? getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' }) matches accessible name: either aria-label or associated label. The label text is \"Project name\". Should work.\n\nMaybe the test fails because the server doesn't serve index.html for path '/' due to fallback logic: In requestHandler, for url.pathname === '/' we set filePath = path.join(process.cwd(),'public','index.html')? Actually condition: if (url.pathname === '/' || url.pathname.endsWith('/')) { filePath = ... } That works.\n\nBut earlier they have a comment // Serve static files; fallback to index.html for SPA routes. Might be fine.\n\nOne failure: test 001 health and project creation persist on reload: they timed out waiting for heading. Could be that server not started when tests run because they spawn npm start but maybe they need to wait for server to be ready. In our server we log and listen. That's okay.\n\nBut maybe the test uses PORT environment variable set to something else, and our server binds to that, fine.\n\nHowever they timed out on heading, meaning page didn't load at all. Could be because the server crashed after first request due to SQLite usage of sync API which might block event loop? But sync API should be okay.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the server process exits after first request due to unhandled promise rejection? In handleApi for POST, we return getJsonBody(req).then(...). That's okay.\n\nBut maybe the DB file path not persisted across restarts because DB_PATH defaults to cwd/workboard.db which is fine. Persistence test after reload means they reload page (same server) not restart.\n\nBut test 011 seed process-restart persistence checks: they probably kill and restart server. Our server uses sync DB, which persists file. Should work.\n\nThe errors indicate connection refused when page.goto after process restart. Means server didn't start on new port? The test likely restarts server by killing and rerunning npm start. Our server uses DB_PATH env maybe not set; but it's fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that server doesn't close previous DB before process exit leading to lock file, causing next start to fail to open DB? SQLite sync Database may lock file and not allow new connection until closed. On process exit, file should be closed automatically.\n\nBut maybe when server restarts quickly, the DB file is still locked causing error and server crashes. Need to add handling to close DB on exit? Not required.\n\nGiven time, perhaps simpler: tests failing because our HTML uses single quotes inside template literals causing backticks? No.\n\nActually test 001 health failed because they couldn't find heading; that could be because page didn't load due to 404 fallback? Our fallback for unknown routes loads index.html but for '/' we already serve static index.html. Should be fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the server returns HTML but with content-type maybe not correct? Not needed.\n\nCould be that Playwright expects button with name 'Create project' role button. Our button id 'create-btn' text 'Create project' fine.\n\nPotential missing: The project rows need data-testid=\"project-row\" visible. We have that.\n\nMaybe the issue is that after creating project, they reload page, expecting row visible. Our createProject function triggers POST then renderList. Works.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the server's GET /api/projects returns rows ordered by id, fine.\n\nGiven unknown, maybe the server is not started in test environment because npm start may not use correct working directory? It's fine.\n\nLet's run Playwright test locally? Hard.\n\nGiven time, maybe the health endpoint path is wrong: they call GET /health expecting JSON. Our server returns JSON correctly.\n\nBut the test timed out on heading, not health. Health test earlier succeeded? They didn't show health failure.\n\nThus maybe the server didn't serve root due to missing trailing slash handling: requestHandler when url.pathname === '/' or endsWith('/') sets filePath to index.html. That's fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that our index.html includes a comment with backticks causing syntax error in script? The comment includes backticks inside template literal string? In HTML, we have a comment with backticks inside JS template literal backticks: `getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' })`. This is inside an HTML comment, not JS. Should be fine.\n\nPotentially the script fails because of backticks in comment interfering with template literal? The comment is inside backticks of the template string assigned to app.innerHTML. Inside that string we have backticks delimiting the template literal. Inside the string we have backticks inside comment: ``getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' })``? Actually comment line: `\u003c!-- The input receives an explicit ARIA label so that Playwright's `getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' })` can locate it reliably across browsers. --\u003e` This includes backticks inside HTML comment, which will close the outer template literal? The outer backticks are the ones used to define app.innerHTML string: app.innerHTML = ` ... `. Inside that string, there are backticks inside the comment, which will terminate the string early causing syntax error. Indeed JavaScript template literals cannot contain unescaped backticks. This will cause a runtime error, preventing page rendering, leading to no heading.\n\nThus need to escape backticks or remove them. Remove that comment with backticks or replace backticks with single quotes.\n\nLet's modify index.html: replace backticks around getByRole with single quotes or escape.\n\nAlso other comment lines may have backticks. Search.","id":"rs_478700","summary":[{"text":"Everything seems correct. Why tests timed out? Possibly because Playwright expects elements to have role attributes. The heading \u003ch1\u003e default role heading, fine.\n\nBut maybe the root page not loaded due to SPA navigation interfering with Playwright navigation? They navigate to '/' and then expect heading visible. That should be fine.\n\nThe test also expects that after creating project and reload, the row persists. That should work.\n\nPotential issue: In index.html, the input has aria-label but also label element with for attribute. Role textbox detection uses label text? getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' }) matches accessible name: either aria-label or associated label. The label text is \"Project name\". Should work.\n\nMaybe the test fails because the server doesn't serve index.html for path '/' due to fallback logic: In requestHandler, for url.pathname === '/' we set filePath = path.join(process.cwd(),'public','index.html')? Actually condition: if (url.pathname === '/' || url.pathname.endsWith('/')) { filePath = ... } That works.\n\nBut earlier they have a comment // Serve static files; fallback to index.html for SPA routes. Might be fine.\n\nOne failure: test 001 health and project creation persist on reload: they timed out waiting for heading. Could be that server not started when tests run because they spawn npm start but maybe they need to wait for server to be ready. In our server we log and listen. That's okay.\n\nBut maybe the test uses PORT environment variable set to something else, and our server binds to that, fine.\n\nHowever they timed out on heading, meaning page didn't load at all. Could be because the server crashed after first request due to SQLite usage of sync API which might block event loop? But sync API should be okay.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the server process exits after first request due to unhandled promise rejection? In handleApi for POST, we return getJsonBody(req).then(...). That's okay.\n\nBut maybe the DB file path not persisted across restarts because DB_PATH defaults to cwd/workboard.db which is fine. Persistence test after reload means they reload page (same server) not restart.\n\nBut test 011 seed process-restart persistence checks: they probably kill and restart server. Our server uses sync DB, which persists file. Should work.\n\nThe errors indicate connection refused when page.goto after process restart. Means server didn't start on new port? The test likely restarts server by killing and rerunning npm start. Our server uses DB_PATH env maybe not set; but it's fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that server doesn't close previous DB before process exit leading to lock file, causing next start to fail to open DB? SQLite sync Database may lock file and not allow new connection until closed. On process exit, file should be closed automatically.\n\nBut maybe when server restarts quickly, the DB file is still locked causing error and server crashes. Need to add handling to close DB on exit? Not required.\n\nGiven time, perhaps simpler: tests failing because our HTML uses single quotes inside template literals causing backticks? No.\n\nActually test 001 health failed because they couldn't find heading; that could be because page didn't load due to 404 fallback? Our fallback for unknown routes loads index.html but for '/' we already serve static index.html. Should be fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the server returns HTML but with content-type maybe not correct? Not needed.\n\nCould be that Playwright expects button with name 'Create project' role button. Our button id 'create-btn' text 'Create project' fine.\n\nPotential missing: The project rows need data-testid=\"project-row\" visible. We have that.\n\nMaybe the issue is that after creating project, they reload page, expecting row visible. Our createProject function triggers POST then renderList. Works.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the server's GET /api/projects returns rows ordered by id, fine.\n\nGiven unknown, maybe the server is not started in test environment because npm start may not use correct working directory? It's fine.\n\nLet's run Playwright test locally? Hard.\n\nGiven time, maybe the health endpoint path is wrong: they call GET /health expecting JSON. Our server returns JSON correctly.\n\nBut the test timed out on heading, not health. Health test earlier succeeded? They didn't show health failure.\n\nThus maybe the server didn't serve root due to missing trailing slash handling: requestHandler when url.pathname === '/' or endsWith('/') sets filePath to index.html. That's fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that our index.html includes a comment with backticks causing syntax error in script? The comment includes backticks inside template literal string? In HTML, we have a comment with backticks inside JS template literal backticks: `getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' })`. This is inside an HTML comment, not JS. Should be fine.\n\nPotentially the script fails because of backticks in comment interfering with template literal? The comment is inside backticks of the template string assigned to app.innerHTML. Inside that string we have backticks delimiting the template literal. Inside the string we have backticks inside comment: ``getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' })``? Actually comment line: `\u003c!-- The input receives an explicit ARIA label so that Playwright's `getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name' })` can locate it reliably across browsers. --\u003e` This includes backticks inside HTML comment, which will close the outer template literal? The outer backticks are the ones used to define app.innerHTML string: app.innerHTML = ` ... `. Inside that string, there are backticks inside the comment, which will terminate the string early causing syntax error. Indeed JavaScript template literals cannot contain unescaped backticks. This will cause a runtime error, preventing page rendering, leading to no heading.\n\nThus need to escape backticks or remove them. Remove that comment with backticks or replace backticks with single quotes.\n\nLet's modify index.html: replace backticks around getByRole with single quotes or escape.\n\nAlso other comment lines may have backticks. Search.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"arguments":"{\"cmd\":\"grep -n \\\"`\\\" -n public/index.html\",\"sandbox_permissions\":\"use_default\",\"timeout\":10000,\"tty\":false,\"workdir\":\"/home/agent/work\"}","call_id":"call_hid8c1gc","id":"fc_539670_0","name":"exec_command","status":"completed","type":"function_call"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"reasoning":{"effort":"medium","summary":"auto"},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","status":"completed","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"}},"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"type":"function","name":"exec_command","description":"Runs a command in a PTY, returning output or a session ID for ongoing interaction.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cmd":{"description":"Shell command to execute.","type":"string"},"justification":{"description":"User-facing approval question for `require_escalated`; omit otherwise.","type":"string"},"login":{"description":"True runs the shell with -l/-i semantics; false disables them. Defaults to true.","type":"boolean"},"max_output_tokens":{"description":"Output token budget. Defaults to 10000 tokens; larger requests may be capped by policy.","type":"number"},"prefix_rule":{"description":"Reusable approval prefix for `cmd`, only with `sandbox_permissions: \"require_escalated\"`; for example [\"git\", \"pull\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"sandbox_permissions":{"description":"Per-command sandbox override. Defaults to `use_default`; use `require_escalated` for unsandboxed execution.","enum":["use_default","require_escalated"],"type":"string"},"shell":{"description":"Shell binary to launch. Defaults to the user's default shell.","type":"string"},"tty":{"description":"True allocates a PTY for the command; false or omitted uses plain pipes.","type":"boolean"},"workdir":{"description":"Working directory for the command. Defaults to the turn cwd.","type":"string"},"yield_time_ms":{"description":"Wait before yielding output. Defaults to 10000 ms; effective range is 250-30000 ms.","type":"number"}},"required":["cmd"],"type":"object"}},{"type":"function","name":"write_stdin","description":"Writes characters to an existing unified exec session and returns recent output.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"chars":{"description":"Bytes to write to stdin. Defaults to empty, which polls without writing.","type":"string"},"max_output_tokens":{"description":"Output token budget. Defaults to 10000 tokens; larger requests may be capped by policy.","type":"number"},"session_id":{"description":"Identifier of the running unified exec session.","type":"number"},"yield_time_ms":{"description":"Wait before yielding output. Non-empty writes default to 250 ms and cap at 30000 ms; empty polls wait 5000-300000 ms by default.","type":"number"}},"required":["session_id"],"type":"object"}},{"type":"function","name":"request_user_input","description":"Request user input for one to three short questions and wait for the response. This tool is only available in Plan mode.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"questions":{"description":"Questions to show the user. Prefer 1 and do not exceed 3","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"header":{"description":"Short header label shown in the UI (12 or fewer chars).","type":"string"},"id":{"description":"Stable identifier for mapping answers (snake_case).","type":"string"},"options":{"description":"Provide 2-3 mutually exclusive choices. Put the recommended option first and suffix its label with \"(Recommended)\". Do not include an \"Other\" option in this list; the client will add a free-form \"Other\" option automatically.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"description":{"description":"One short sentence explaining impact/tradeoff if selected.","type":"string"},"label":{"description":"User-facing label (1-5 words).","type":"string"}},"required":["label","description"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"question":{"description":"Single-sentence prompt shown to the user.","type":"string"}},"required":["id","header","question","options"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"}},"required":["questions"],"type":"object"}},{"type":"function","name":"view_image","description":"View a local image file from the filesystem when visual inspection is needed. Use this for images already available on disk.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path":{"description":"Local filesystem path to an image file.","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"}},{"type":"function","name":"get_goal","description":"Get the current goal for this thread, including status, budgets, token and elapsed-time usage, and remaining token budget.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"type":"function","name":"create_goal","description":"Create a goal only when explicitly requested by the user or system/developer instructions; do not infer goals from ordinary tasks.\nSet token_budget only when an explicit token budget is requested. Fails if an unfinished goal exists; use update_goal only for status.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"objective":{"description":"Required. The concrete objective to start pursuing. This starts a new active goal when no goal exists or replaces the current goal when it is complete.","type":"string"},"token_budget":{"description":"Positive token budget for the new goal. Omit unless explicitly requested.","type":"integer"}},"required":["objective"],"type":"object"}},{"type":"function","name":"update_goal","description":"Update the existing goal.\nSet status to `paused` only at the user's explicit request to pause this goal, never on your own initiative. Ask if unclear; a later resume revokes that request. Report the returned status and stop goal work. Budget limits take precedence over pausing.\nSet status to `complete` only when the objective has actually been achieved and no required work remains.\nSet status to `blocked` only when the same blocking condition has repeated for at least three consecutive goal turns, counting the original/user-triggered turn and any automatic continuations, and the agent cannot make meaningful progress without user input or an external-state change.\nIf the user resumes a goal that was previously marked `blocked`, treat the resumed run as a fresh blocked audit. If the same blocking condition then repeats for at least three consecutive resumed goal turns, set status to `blocked` again.\nOnce the blocked threshold is satisfied, do not keep reporting that you are still blocked while leaving the goal active; set status to `blocked`.\nDo not use `blocked` merely because the work is hard, slow, uncertain, incomplete, or would benefit from clarification.\nDo not mark a goal complete merely because its budget is nearly exhausted or because you are stopping work.\nYou cannot use this tool to resume, budget-limit, or usage-limit a goal; those status changes are controlled by the user or system.\nWhen marking a budgeted goal achieved with status `complete`, report the final token usage from the tool result to the user.","strict":false,"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"status":{"description":"Required. `paused` requires an explicit user request. Set to `complete` only when the objective is achieved and no required work remains. Set to `blocked` only after the same blocking condition has recurred for at least three consecutive goal turns and the agent is at an impasse. After a previously blocked goal is resumed, the resumed run starts a fresh blocked audit.","enum":["complete","blocked","paused"],"type":"string"}},"required":["status"],"type":"object"}}],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":1,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":7700,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":6751},"output_tokens":1297,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0},"total_tokens":8997}},"sequence_number":1248,"type":"response.completed"}
